.MARINE...
(Today through Sunday)
Issued at 926 AM PST Tue Nov 10 2026

Gentle to moderate northerly breezes continue over the coastal
waters through Tuesday night. Southerly winds develop midweek out
ahead of a deepening area of low pressure. Winds increase fresh
to near gale by Friday a the deepening low pressure approaches.
The increasing winds will lead to steep fresh swell. A moderate
sea state will prevail through midweek week, deteriorating
further late Friday and continue over the weekend as northwest
swell builds with a longer period. Mariners with plans late in the
week should monitor the forecast the next few days as dangerous
conditions are expected next weekend.

